title start
kind: default
tags: ecosystem server binary dev-mode
Plan: the ecosystem binary, the one server and dev mode
title end

section start
title start
Section 1: decided by Shape 2026-11-07
title end

paragraph start
One binary called ecosystem covers everything in the ecosystem. Any command such as ecosystem update runs when code changes.
paragraph end

paragraph start
One shared server for the whole ecosystem, written in Rust. Every package can also have its own small server and still works alone.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Dev mode lives in the server. The server runs the new version. If the new version fails, the server kills it and runs the last good one.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The package manager AIU-PM is the base. It must use local files when a package has no upstream.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The package manager itself must be covered by dev mode too.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Later: a bar in the shell shows information about the server. It is in aiu-shell/todo.aiu.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 2: the pieces
title end

paragraph start
The ecosystem binary: Racket front. Commands status, update, serve, dev, stop. It calls the package manager and talks to the server.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The package manager: owns packages, builds, generations and rollback. A generation is a good version, and the last good one is the previous generation, so rollback is a pointer move.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The ecosystem manifest: one list of every package in the ecosystem with its local folder. Local folders are the source when there is no upstream.
paragraph end

paragraph start
The server: holds the notation database, the name registry and the list of running programs with their modes. Dev supervisor inside it: build the new version, start it, health check, keep it or kill it and return to the last good generation.
paragraph end

paragraph start
ecosystem update: fingerprint every package folder, rebuild only the changed ones through the package manager, make a new generation, tell the server.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 3: order of work
title end

paragraph start
The order is the order of the to-do in todo.aiu at the ecosystem root. Finished items are deleted from the to-do in the same script, so the next AI continues from the first item left.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Section 4: still open
title end

paragraph start
The protocol between a package and a server, and how packages find the shared server.
paragraph end

paragraph start
How a package switches between its own server and the shared one, and what happens when the shared one goes away.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Who owns the name registry, and how names stay unique across all packages.
paragraph end

paragraph start
What a health check is for each kind of program: editor, multiplexer, shell, server.
paragraph end

section end

